<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is Spain's snap election being rigged? Debunking viral claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d874ff70cb3a8a6b114cf5a70ad83a27627debecd4b926c13fb8824017e8e830</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T22:17:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261126-is-spain-s-snap-election-being-rigged-debunking-viral-claims--7ddac706223a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261126-is-spain-s-snap-election-being-rigged-debunking-viral-claims" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Spain's snap election on Sunday, allegations of vote rigging - known in Spanish as "pucherazo" - are spreading widely on social media. From claims that undocumented migrants are being illegally registered to vote, to allegations that postal ballots and vote counts could be manipulated, internet users are accusing Pedro Sánchez's government of attempting to rig the election. But these claims misrepresent how Spain's electoral system works, as Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Citizens angry with the establishment' as Spain heads to the polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44d06c489df8a9b3c865964f95ef43e9d880a501f114ecdbae583e87103dccbf</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T22:16:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261126-citizens-angry-with-the-establishment-as-spain-heads-to-the-polls--da4ec16b4e85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261126-citizens-angry-with-the-establishment-as-spain-heads-to-the-polls" /><summary type="html">Three party leaders are vying in Spain's general election on Sunday, which leftist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez called following a parliamentary setback over housing legislation that underscored the fragility of his minority coalition government. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Javier Carbonell, Policy Analyst at the European Policy Centre, says that despite solid economic growth in Spain the population "have suffered a housing crisis and inflation, citizens are still angry with the government and the economic system regardless of macroeconomic data", adding that "in the end citizens are angry with the establishment, in this case it will be Sanchez, but to be honest I think they will be angry at PP and Vox very soon".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>'Citizens angry with the establishment' as Spain heads to the polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26a436c4c79db714c8ba64cacfbc75bcfcd56e86827e46e8f54258c5188437fa</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T22:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/citizens-angry-with-the-establishment-as-spain-heads-to-the-polls--6736d3f3f0d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/citizens-angry-with-the-establishment-as-spain-heads-to-the-polls" /><summary type="html">Three party leaders are vying in Spain's general election on Sunday, which leftist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez called following a parliamentary setback over housing legislation that underscored the fragility of his minority coalition government. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Javier Carbonell, Policy Analyst at the European Policy Centre, says that despite solid economic growth in Spain the population "have suffered a housing crisis and inflation, citizens are still angry with the government and the economic system regardless of macroeconomic data",  adding that "in the end citizens are angry with the establishment, in this case it will be Sanchez, but to be honest I think they will be angry at PP and Vox very soon".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump urges Putin to end 'military aggression' in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23e3a483d326d94b2b861eba4992c5106f99f8d240dc8aedd2308c00e6ae9849</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:10:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-urges-putin-to-end-military-aggression-in-europe--83da6f6c9073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-urges-putin-to-end-military-aggression-in-europe" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Thursday he had asked Vladimir Putin to "pull back all military aggression" against Europe, in a shift in tone towards the leader Russian he called his friend just a week ago. Trump said he had made the request to Putin when they met in China last week, adding that he thought it would help lead to a deal to end Moscow's grinding war in Ukraine. The US leader's comments come a day after he hosted NATO chief Mark Rutte in Florida, after which they issued a joint statement calling on Russia not to expand the Ukraine war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Le Pen slams push for EU budget deal before French election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6ec914a1d08f6bc91c1e3f482bff3858a472089add9023aedeea011beae540b</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/le-pen-slams-push-for-eu-budget-deal-before-french-election--6a2142c22baf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-slams-push-for-eu-budget-deal-before-french-election" /><summary type="html">EU leaders locked horns over the bloc's budget at a summit meeting in Brussels on Thursday, as far-right leader Marine Le Pen slammed an "underhanded" push to lock in the long-term spending plans before French presidential elections next year. European Council head Antonio Costa turned up the pressure upon arrival at the budget talks, where heavyweight Germany is pressing for cuts as well as burden-sharing on money for Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Spain's far right replace Europe's left-wing stalwart?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3003ca370b49de8edec97fda4fd9cde660522b5b83d4cecb8d4aeb24b3aee353</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T16:51:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-will-spain-s-far-right-replace-europe-s-left-wing-stalwart--db04554adc61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-will-spain-s-far-right-replace-europe-s-left-wing-stalwart" /><summary type="html">Some 39 million Spaniards will head to the ballot this Sunday to vote in early general elections. Latest polls put the conservative Popular Party ahead of incumbent PM Pedro Sanchez’s Socialists. The third-strongest political force, however, is the far-right Vox party. A strong showing at Sunday’s election could see them form Spain’s next government. FRANCE 24 explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spanish economist de Cos to succeed Lagarde as head of ECB</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af834a28f0f4fe8f093a7cfb9288eece69ea3c09505de9406db26891616f08d2</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:55:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-spanish-economist-de-cos-succeed-lagarde-head-ecb--8f2ca94f4b4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-spanish-economist-de-cos-succeed-lagarde-head-ecb" /><summary type="html">Spanish monetary economist Pablo Hernandez de Cos on Thursday was set to replace France's Christine Lagarde as the new head of the European Central Bank (ECB). His nomination comes as the Europe's most powerful financial institution grapples with an Iran war-driven resurgence in inflation and a cost of living crisis.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>How far-right Vox is winning over young voters ahead of Spain's snap election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dbcfd37f5fefa4586b3514fdf365c982ec6319a27f7244462542f47fa60e352</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:37:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-how-far-right-vox-winning-over-young-voters-ahead-spain-snap-election--47f59a2e1b12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-how-far-right-vox-winning-over-young-voters-ahead-spain-snap-election" /><summary type="html">Spain's Vox party is winning over many young people ahead of the country's snap election on November 29, particularly men. The far-right party is capitalising on the rising cost of living and anti-immigrant sentiment to expand its once-marginal electoral base.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Housing crisis on the ballot: Anger boils over ahead of Spanish election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:140d8300a44834c9d5ea585dfa6d5b90693366c8413bce859f779102bcd841de</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:33:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261126-housing-crisis-on-the-ballot-anger-boils-over-ahead-of-spanish-election--8ce61f9ccb88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261126-housing-crisis-on-the-ballot-anger-boils-over-ahead-of-spanish-election" /><summary type="html">Spaniards head to the polls on Sunday in a general election that was called after street protests for affordable housing. Anger bubbled over after 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal was evicted from her home of seven decades and two decrees to tackle the housing crisis were rejected by parliament. In calling the snap election, Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is hoping the housing issue can galvanise his left-wing base.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>'Europe has two kinds of countries: Small countries &amp; those that haven’t yet realised they’re small’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:918de94fce86bca76d2130c97887d63935f6fb550abc18dbf79e3e8f1604ca5f</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:31:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-has-two-kinds-of-countries-small-countries-those-that-haven-t-yet-realised-they-re-small--670c576b786b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-has-two-kinds-of-countries-small-countries-those-that-haven-t-yet-realised-they-re-small" /><summary type="html">“The implications of having the far right in power in Brussels are enormous,” warns Sophie Pornschlegel, Senior Advisor at the European Policy Centre. With elections approaching in several EU member states, including France and Italy, what would a growing number of far-right, Eurosceptic governments mean for the EU budget, relations between European institutions, common legislation and support for Ukraine? Could Giorgia Meloni could adopt a more radical stance? “The whole idea of the EU is to have a common legislation that is then applied in 27 member states. Otherwise, what is the point of having the EU?”</summary></entry><entry><title>EU leaders face showdown over Ukraine funding as divisions deepen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19beeabe6aa1094c0418ce4658063aa836ff585db30302ebe433d687e5b21196</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:56:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen--870d4c5e802d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen" /><summary type="html">European Union leaders on Thursday are set to tackle deep divisions as they meet in Brussels to discuss the bloc's long-term budget in Brussels, which includes a proposed €45 billion loan to keep Ukraine funded through 2027.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Ukraine has ‘no intention’ of extending war to Libya, FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1cc4a3d9389cf75f72feaba052d12c7b1bf581237c8ef04e13a944c1dff0132</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T05:44:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-live-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen--a294d556357d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-live-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen" /><summary type="html">Ukraine was not attempting to spread the war with Russia to Libyan shores by attacking two Russian ships off the coast of Benghazi, Kyiv's Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga said Thursday, shortly after a phone call with his Libyan counterpart. The attack in the Mediterranean has sparked fears that the war was expanding beyond European front lines. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU says 'strongly' rejects premise of new US tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dab0dc424dd1d490a5f3ce1fc9252c36591eca5803fa0b554682c5c2abac3b88</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:43:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T19:48:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-says-strongly-rejects-premise-of-new-us-tariffs--7c46a79d798f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-strongly-rejects-premise-of-new-us-tariffs" /><summary type="html">The EU said Wednesday that it rejected the premise of new tariffs on its exports proposed by the United States and expected Washington to stick by a deal struck with Brussels last year. The US unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland says will create no-fly zone at Ukraine border after repeated airspace violations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc7ea223d365244d8b35c21128d5131072fa17b6fdb261a67f7b3c27ccac8def</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T19:22:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-says-will-create-no-fly-zone-at-ukraine-border-after-repeated-airspace-violations--7fab10c8802f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-says-will-create-no-fly-zone-at-ukraine-border-after-repeated-airspace-violations" /><summary type="html">Poland will soon create a no-fly zone near the Ukrainian border, a deputy defence minister announced on Wednesday, after several incursions into its airspace it blamed on Russia. Poland backs Ukraine as it fights off Russia's near five-year invasion and has repeatedly accused Moscow of seeking to target Kyiv's supporters with drone incursions and other methods. The no-fly zone is intended to allow Polish forces to quickly identify any Russian military aircraft and shoot them down if necessary. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Turkey's deadly factory blast: 'Investing in safety costs more than letting people die'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3a4b98f70880a575974477e312b45b0321f8eea2bc41c2de3dec74a1d9815e1</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T17:28:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-factory-blast-turkey-izmir--11e9146de7c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-factory-blast-turkey-izmir" /><summary type="html">An explosion at a steel factory on November 9 in Turkey's Aliaga, near Izmir, killed 19 people. This tragedy follows several others and highlights the issues surrounding workers’ safety in Turkey, our Observers say. They also condemn the repressive responses from the government and the company.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Moldova launches national preparedness campaign after drone incursions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0874ac1baaa022feaf368fc34f68c183e5dce7a6c29f2e57fe857f6cbbe7d4df</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:34:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/moldova-launches-national-preparedness-campaign-after-drone-incursions--b8c5b821eb8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/moldova-launches-national-preparedness-campaign-after-drone-incursions" /><summary type="html">Moldova is urging its citizens to prepare for emergencies as the war in neighbouring Ukraine brings new risks across its border. The “Moldova Ready” campaign, launched in Chisinau, includes a display of the remains of a drone carrying 52kg of explosives after it crashed in the country last month. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kremlin declines comment on reports 700,000 Russian soldiers killed in Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b190d5cc275c6f5e9c747869c1d24c39dfd649b085c9e8753f2d6d32c2bf8e3</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:14:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-kremlin-declines-comment-reports-700-000-russian-soldiers-killed-ukraine-war--97c7af478f38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-kremlin-declines-comment-reports-700-000-russian-soldiers-killed-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov on Wednesday declined to comment on reports in Russian and international news outlets that around 700,000 Russian soldiers have been killed in the Ukraine war so far. The reports were based on hacked data from Russia's official statistics agency. Peskov said only the defence ministry can disclose figures and told reporters "not to pay attention to any other data".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Surprise Eurostar strike cancels London, Paris and Brussels trains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18d6d31f0fe70eaa24792a9e56d1236197e87fdb98d38dc4ed89dd99f4b9bb72</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:02:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-surprise-eurostar-strike-cancels-london-paris-and-brussels-trains--87744ac1110c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-surprise-eurostar-strike-cancels-london-paris-and-brussels-trains" /><summary type="html">Several Eurostar trains connecting London, Paris and Brussels were cancelled in a surprise strike on Wednesday. The train operator did not specify who exactly was striking or the reasons why.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Two Libyan soldiers killed in Ukrainian attack on Russian vessels in Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c479bb3c2b3fed28863aa9ee60e3e079b954a9a84acd38285af365b2280f420</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T03:46:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-live-two-libyan-soldiers-killed-in-ukrainian-attack-on-russian-vessels-in-benghazi--3e3be77f4806.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-live-two-libyan-soldiers-killed-in-ukrainian-attack-on-russian-vessels-in-benghazi" /><summary type="html">Two Libyan soldiers have died from wounds sustained in an attack, claimed by Ukraine, on Russian ships near Benghazi, a senior figure in the administration in eastern Libya said late on Tuesday. Members of the European Parliament will convene in Strasbourg Wednesday to discuss "Europe’s role and capacity to protect the international order and secure a just and lasting peace for Ukraine". Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine seeks €115 billion in foreign aid for 2027, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d37ebaad83ca117d8e916f57bbe6410f66130cf8492c0e7fb1123a8f849f11</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T01:19:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-ukraine-seeks-_115-billion-in-foreign-aid-for-2027-zelensky-says--06c01a5e24b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-ukraine-seeks-%E2%82%AC115-billion-in-foreign-aid-for-2027-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukraine will need €115 billion in external financing next year to sustain its economy and war effort against Russia, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday, adding that Kyiv had secured commitments for about €90 billion from the European Union.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian nuclear satellites plan 'foolhardy', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf0837f53bafff9128522242cc3b7cdb622a0e96f3bdd7bdb028e6222d227da</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T20:31:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says--a17887817d5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. Speaking to FRANCE 24, Dafydd Townley, Senior Teaching Fellow in International Security at the University of Portsmouth, says that the alleged plan would be "foolhardy because the impact would be indiscriminate, they wouldn't be able to choose only Western or non-Russian satellites".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian losses on Ukrainian front top 700,000 including missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d5175f0d8594e449f2a1234c912a6388073dfcd0199be4aac1586488bf324c</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T19:22:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing--6a745520bcf6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing" /><summary type="html">New analysis of leaked Russian government data suggests more than 700,000 Russian soldiers have died in the war against Ukraine. Independent Russian media outlets have updated their estimates of Moscow's military casualties, including soldiers missing on the frontline, after Belarusian and Ukrainian hackers obtained figures from the Russian statistics agency. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Both sides are prepared to operate outside of the conflict zone'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71f0bb454d8938d49e21a9c6a3fa9aa50a682458cb247a034010bf2936c5bfad</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T17:26:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone--766d3b319486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone" /><summary type="html">Charli James is pleased to welcome Gavin Hall, Teaching Fellow in Political Science, and International Security at the University of Strathclyde. Hall examines recent Russian and Ukrainian operations beyond the main conflict zone, the conditions necessary for a negotiated settlement and the implications of diminishing direct US military support for Ukraine. “Both sides are prepared to operate beyond the main battleground and outside of the conflict zone,” he explains. Hall discusses why both sides want to negotiate from a position of strength and the conditions under which a “mutually hurting stalemate” could lead to a negotiated settlement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin says Ukraine still hits Russian oil plants despite Trump's requests to stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20ed5a5645739b074444aa2078e6f72c68705a62f51d086fdf0d548ab3261610</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:50:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters--e55baa58ddf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters" /><summary type="html">Ukraine continues attacks on Russian oil refineries despite requests from US President ​Donald Trump to ‌withhold them, Russian leader Vladimir Putin said Tuesday, pledging to ⁠retaliate. Kyiv has said it would not stop targeting Russian energy targets until Moscow had done the same. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges four-way peace talks with Russia, Europe and US 'as soon as possible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43b4e07cd0c74f4ba98297d82efc7f022c94f9f08d1e4c0da52dd0f4b5dcf1c9</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T00:30:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible--354e3c5e6ad8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is calling for a new round of negotiations involving Ukraine, Russia, the United States and European leaders, saying Kyiv is ready to meet as early as Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO vows space defence after Russia nuclear satellite report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46212584cdad6ab6909c10d4f503da5db0a65f85278331f0cca36cccf331b3b3</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:33:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report--b818d8d38eb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. The media reports, citing unnamed German military and BND spy agency sources, said Moscow was thought to be planning such a launch in the coming weeks, giving it the capability to destroy other satellites. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: 'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd15502ebc9c1d40c40d5f5c7cd9f4e2932e559e3b4fa332a0c6c7c2b1acc80</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--b335b8ca1842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drone attacks and long-range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: 'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8adb09184945de3e75bfb16c5a260fd784cefa899d6fe5fe94333efc57056d76</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--4945328f5666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drone attacks and long-range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya's east seeks UN probe into claims Ukrainian military present in west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd2252ac1b20ebd7bedb62eba41411b60efdd7a17ba62c60a3e4153b615641a2</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T20:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west--6cb055560ea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west" /><summary type="html">Authorities in divided Libya's east called on Monday for the United Nations to investigate claims that Ukrainian forces were present in the country's west, as they lodged a complaint over Ukrainian attacks on two Russian ships off Benghazi. The strikes on Sunday, claimed by Kyiv, come as Ukraine steps up strikes against Russia far from the front lines of their war. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims it sank Russian warship off Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1335987e61b434f0740997d307b5db836b953a749d86f258e07fe423fd0f4bd2</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya--1e8645cf71f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya" /><summary type="html">Ukraine on Monday claimed it was behind strikes on two Russian vessels off Libya, including one that sank a modern warship, in the latest spillover from Moscow's invasion. The attacks on Sunday near the Libyan port of Benghazi come at a time when Ukraine has stepped up its daring strikes against Russia far from the frontlines in retaliation for Moscow's deadly invasion. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry></feed>
